<section class="panel"><span class="number">SETUP COMPLETE</span><h2>Class is officially out.</h2><p>The database and 1,000 Sissy Bot accounts are installed. The installer is locked.</p><ol><li>Keep <strong>Apache and MySQL</strong> running in XAMPP.</li><li>Double-click <code>bin\start-bots.cmd</code> and keep that window open. This keeps the community playing even when all browsers are closed.</li><li>Enter the playground and create your fighter account.</li></ol><p>Use <code>bin\stop-bots.cmd</code> for a clean worker stop. When the worker is off, visiting the game can advance matches; it cannot run unattended.</p><a class="button" href="index.php">ENTER THE PLAYGROUND →</a></section>
<?php else:?>
<section class="panel"><span class="number">01 / CHECK THE BELL</span><h2>Ready to rumble?</h2><div class="checks"><?php foreach($checks as $name=>$ok):?><div class="check <?=$ok?'':'bad'?>"><?=$ok?'✓':'✕'?> <?=esc($name)?></div><?php endforeach;?></div><p>In XAMPP Control Panel, start <strong>Apache</strong> and <strong>MySQL</strong>. The default local XAMPP database user is <code>root</code> with an empty password unless you changed it.</p></section>
<form class="panel" method="post" autocomplete="off"><span class="number">02 / BUILD THE PLAYGROUND</span><h2>Database connection</h2><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<?=esc((string)$_SESSION['csrf'])?>"><div class="grid">
<label>MySQL host<input name="db_host" value="<?=esc($values['db_host'])?>" required></label><label>MySQL port<input name="db_port" type="number" min="1" max="65535" value="<?=esc($values['db_port'])?>" required></label><label>Database name<input name="db_name" value="<?=esc($values['db_name'])?>" required pattern="[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,64}"></label><label>MySQL username<input name="db_user" value="<?=esc($values['db_user'])?>" required></label><label>MySQL password<input name="db_pass" type="password" value="" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="Leave blank for stock local XAMPP"></label></div><small>Choose a completely empty database. Setup will create it if permitted and refuses databases that already contain any tables. The database password is stored only in the protected app/config.php file.</small><button type="submit" <?=in_array(false,$checks,true)?'disabled':''?>>INSTALL SISSY FIGHTS NXT →</button></form>
<?php endif;?><p><small>Local installation only. No account, cloud service, Node.js, Redis, Composer or API key required.</small></p></main></body></html>
